IMPORT prelude

-- Penal Code 1871 (Singapore) -- the offences an individual most meets and what a conviction under them can cost: age (ss 82, 83),
-- "dishonestly" (ss 23, 24) and "fraudulently" (s 25), theft and its punishment (ss 378 to 381), cheating and its punishment (ss 415,
-- 416B, 417, 420), hurt and grievous hurt and their punishment (ss 319 to 326, 334 to 335), criminal intimidation (ss 503, 506, 507),
-- the right of private defence of the body (ss 96, 97(a), 98, 101 to 103, 106A), and the punishment of an attempt (s 512).
--
-- SEAT: the accused person -- the individual whose act is measured against an offence in the Code and who may be convicted and
-- punished under it. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at 09 Sep 2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt
-- (amendments to Act 21 of 2025, in force 30 December 2025, shown).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Everything else in the Code: the other offences (robbery, extortion, criminal breach of trust, misappropriation, the
-- homicide and sexual offences, and the rest), the general exceptions other than ss 82 and 83 (mistake, accident, unsoundness of
-- mind, intoxication, necessity, consent), private defence of property (ss 104 to 106), abetment, conspiracy and common intention,
-- the enhanced penalties (ss 73 to 74D, among them twice the maximum against a vulnerable person under s 74A), cheating under ss 418
-- and 419, and s 420A. The provisos to Exception 1 of s 300, which ss 334 to 335 borrow, are not encoded: whether the provocation
-- qualifies is the court's finding, taken as an input. Where a section says only "with fine", the Code deposited here states no
-- maximum; this encoding says so and does not supply one. Jurisdiction (ss 2 to 4B) is out. The Code lays prohibitions on the
-- individual, not duties with deadlines, so no regulative rule is written.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Penal Code 1871 -- offences and punishment`

§§ `ss 82, 83 -- my age`

-- s 82: "Nothing is an offence which is done by a child below 10 years of age."
-- s 83: nor by a child "of or above 10 years and below 12, who has not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the
-- nature and consequence of his conduct on that occasion". Whether that maturity was attained is the court's finding: an input.
GIVEN `my age in completed years when I did it` IS A NUMBER,
      `the court finds I had sufficient maturity of understanding to judge the nature and consequence of my conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I did no offence because of my age` IF
        `my age in completed years when I did it` LESS THAN 10
    OR      `my age in completed years when I did it` AT LEAST 10
        AND `my age in completed years when I did it` LESS THAN 12
        AND NOT `the court finds I had sufficient maturity of understanding to judge the nature and consequence of my conduct`

§§ `ss 23, 24, 25 -- dishonestly and fraudulently`

-- s 23(1): a "wrongful gain" is gain "by unlawful means of property to which the person gaining it is not legally entitled", or
-- avoiding a loss one is not entitled to avoid; (2) a "wrongful loss" is loss "by unlawful means of property to which the person
-- losing it ... is legally entitled". Explanation 1: keeping wrongfully, and being kept out of property, count.
-- s 24: I act "dishonestly" if (a) I intend wrongful gain to me or another, or wrongful loss to another, "regardless of whether such
-- gain or loss is temporary or permanent"; or (b) the act "is dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons"
-- and I know it is dishonest by those standards. Limb (b)'s standard is the court's to apply: an input. "Legally entitled" is a
-- term the Code borrows from the general law: asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My intention as to property` HAS
    `I intended someone to gain or keep property, or someone to lose it or be kept out of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by unlawful means` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the one gaining was not legally entitled to it, or the one losing was` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds the act dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I knew it was dishonest by those standards` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN i IS A `My intention as to property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I intend wrongful gain or wrongful loss` i IF
        i's `I intended someone to gain or keep property, or someone to lose it or be kept out of it`
    AND i's `by unlawful means`
    AND i's `the one gaining was not legally entitled to it, or the one losing was`

GIVEN i IS A `My intention as to property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I act dishonestly` i IF
        `Did I intend wrongful gain or wrongful loss` i
    OR      i's `the court finds the act dishonest by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons`
        AND i's `I knew it was dishonest by those standards`

-- s 25: I act "fraudulently" if I act "with intent to deceive" another and by that deception that "an advantage should accrue" to me
-- or another or "detriment should befall" them or another. Explanation 1: not where the advantage or detriment is "so slight that no
-- reasonable person of ordinary sense or temper would complain of it" -- the court's judgment, an input.
GIVEN `I intended to deceive` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I intended by the deception an advantage to me or another, or a detriment to them or another` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the court finds it so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I act fraudulently` IF
        `I intended to deceive`
    AND `I intended by the deception an advantage to me or another, or a detriment to them or another`
    AND NOT `the court finds it so slight that no reasonable person would complain`

§§ `The punishment sections, as a table`

-- Where a section says only "with fine", the deposited Code states no maximum. "Shall be punished with imprisonment ... and shall also
-- be liable to fine" makes imprisonment mandatory and the fine optional; "with imprisonment ..., or with fine, or with both" makes
-- neither mandatory.
DECLARE Fine IS ONE OF
    `no fine`
    `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`
    `a fine of up to` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Caning IS ONE OF
    `no caning`
    `caning at the court's discretion`
    `caning of at least` HAS `strokes` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Section IS ONE OF
    `section 323`
    `section 323A`
    `section 324`
    `section 325`
    `section 326`
    `section 334`
    `section 334A`
    `section 335`
    `section 379`
    `section 379A`
    `section 380`
    `section 381`
    `section 417`
    `section 420(1)`
    `section 420(2)`
    `section 506`
    `section 506, threat of death, grievous hurt, fire or a serious offence`

DECLARE Punishment HAS
    `imprisonment for life is possible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the longest term, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment is mandatory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the fine` IS A Fine
    `the caning` IS A Caning

-- s 323 "3 years, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"; s 323A "5 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000,
-- or with both"; s 324 "7 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination"; s 325 "10 years, and shall also be liable to
-- fine or to caning"; s 326 "imprisonment for life, or ... 15 years, and shall also be liable to caning or if he is not sentenced to
-- imprisonment for life, liable to fine"; s 334 "6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"; s 334A "one year, or
-- with fine which may extend to $7,500, or with both"; s 335 "6 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000, or with both";
-- s 379 "3 years, or with fine, or with both"; ss 379A, 380, 381 "7 years, and shall also be liable to fine"; s 417 "3 years, or with
-- fine, or with both"; s 420(1) "10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning or to both"; s 420(2) "10 years and with
-- caning with not less than 6 strokes, and shall also be liable to fine"; s 506 "2 years, or with fine, or with both", and where the
-- threat is of death, grievous hurt, destruction of property by fire, or an offence punishable with death or 7 years or more,
-- "10 years, or with fine, or with both".
GIVEN s IS A Section
GIVETH A Punishment
`the punishment under` s MEANS
    --                                                 life,  months, mandatory, fine,                                         caning
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `section 323`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 36,     FALSE,     `a fine of up to` 5000,                       `no caning`
    WHEN `section 323A` THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 60,     FALSE,     `a fine of up to` 10000,                      `no caning`
    WHEN `section 324`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 84,     FALSE,     `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `caning at the court's discretion`
    WHEN `section 325`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 120,    TRUE,      `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `caning at the court's discretion`
    WHEN `section 326`  THEN `Punishment` OF           TRUE,  180,    TRUE,      `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `caning at the court's discretion`
    WHEN `section 334`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 6,      FALSE,     `a fine of up to` 2500,                       `no caning`
    WHEN `section 334A` THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 12,     FALSE,     `a fine of up to` 7500,                       `no caning`
    WHEN `section 335`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 72,     FALSE,     `a fine of up to` 10000,                      `no caning`
    WHEN `section 379`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 36,     FALSE,     `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `no caning`
    WHEN `section 379A` THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 84,     TRUE,      `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `no caning`
    WHEN `section 380`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 84,     TRUE,      `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `no caning`
    WHEN `section 381`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 84,     TRUE,      `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `no caning`
    WHEN `section 417`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 36,     FALSE,     `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `no caning`
    WHEN `section 420(1)` THEN `Punishment` OF         FALSE, 120,    TRUE,      `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `caning at the court's discretion`
    WHEN `section 420(2)` THEN `Punishment` OF         FALSE, 120,    TRUE,      `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `caning of at least` 6
    WHEN `section 506`  THEN `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 24,     FALSE,     `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `no caning`
    OTHERWISE                `Punishment` OF           FALSE, 120,    FALSE,     `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`,  `no caning`

GIVEN s IS A Section
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for, in months, under` s MEANS
    (`the punishment under` s)'s `the longest term, in months`

GIVEN s IS A Section
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be imprisoned for life under` s IF
    (`the punishment under` s)'s `imprisonment for life is possible`

GIVEN s IS A Section
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court imprison me if I am convicted under` s IF
    (`the punishment under` s)'s `imprisonment is mandatory`

GIVEN s IS A Section
GIVETH A Fine
`What fine can I be made to pay under` s MEANS
    (`the punishment under` s)'s `the fine`

GIVEN s IS A Section
GIVETH A Caning
`Can I be caned under` s MEANS
    (`the punishment under` s)'s `the caning`

§§ `ss 378 to 381 -- theft`

-- s 378: "Whoever, intending to take dishonestly any movable property out of the possession of any person without that person's
-- consent, moves that property in order to such taking, is said to commit theft."
-- Explanation 1: a thing attached to the earth is not movable property, but becomes so "as soon as it is severed"; Explanation 2: a
-- moving by the same act that severs it may be theft. Explanations 3, 4, 6: moving includes removing an obstacle, separating, moving
-- an animal, and transferring intangible property between accounts. Explanation 5: consent "may be express or implied", by the person
-- in possession or anyone with authority. Illustrations (e) and (g): what is not in anyone's possession cannot be taken out of it;
-- Illustration (k): one's own pawned watch can be stolen, for possession, not ownership, is what counts.
DECLARE `My taking` HAS
    `the thing was attached to the earth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my act severed it from the earth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I moved it, or caused it to move, in order to take it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was in another person's possession when I moved it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person in possession, or someone with authority, consented expressly or impliedly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my intention` IS A `My intention as to property`
    `it is a motor vehicle, or a component part attached to one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was in a building, tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a clerk or servant and it was in my employer's possession` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN t IS A `My taking`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it movable property` t IF
        NOT t's `the thing was attached to the earth`
    OR  t's `my act severed it from the earth`

GIVEN t IS A `My taking`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed theft` t IF
        `Was it movable property` t
    AND t's `it was in another person's possession when I moved it`
    AND NOT t's `the person in possession, or someone with authority, consented expressly or impliedly`
    AND `Did I act dishonestly` (t's `my intention`)
    AND t's `I moved it, or caused it to move, in order to take it`

-- s 379 punishes "whoever commits theft"; s 379A theft "of a motor vehicle or any component part of a motor vehicle"; s 380 theft
-- "in any building, tent or vessel ... used as a human dwelling, or for the custody of property"; s 381 theft by "a clerk or servant
-- ... in respect of any property in the possession of his master or employer". More than one may reach the same theft; all are
-- listed.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A Section
GIVETH A LIST OF Section
`only if` b s MEANS IF b THEN LIST s ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN t IS A `My taking`
GIVETH A LIST OF Section
`Which sections can punish my theft` t MEANS
    IF NOT `Have I committed theft` t
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `section 379` FOLLOWED BY
             append (`only if` (t's `it is a motor vehicle, or a component part attached to one`) `section 379A`)
                    (append (`only if` (t's `it was in a building, tent or vessel used as a human dwelling or for the custody of property`) `section 380`)
                            (`only if` (t's `I am a clerk or servant and it was in my employer's possession`) `section 381`))

-- s 379A(2): a person convicted under s 379A "shall, unless the court for special reasons thinks fit to order otherwise, be
-- disqualified ... from holding or obtaining a driving licence", for the period the court orders from release from imprisonment.
GIVEN s IS A Section, `the court for special reasons orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be disqualified from holding a driving licence` IF
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `section 379A` THEN NOT `the court for special reasons orders otherwise`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 415, 416B, 417, 420 -- cheating`

-- s 415: "Whoever, by deceiving any person, whether or not such deception was the sole or main inducement, fraudulently or dishonestly
-- induces the person so deceived to deliver or cause the delivery of any property to any person, or to consent that any person shall
-- retain any property, or intentionally induces the person so deceived to do or omit to do anything which he would not do or omit to
-- do if he were not so deceived, and which act or omission causes or is likely to cause damage or harm to any person in body, mind,
-- reputation or property, is said to 'cheat'." Explanation 1: "A dishonest concealment of facts is a deception". Explanation 2: "Mere
-- breach of contract is not of itself proof of an original fraudulent intent" -- Illustration (g): one who meant to deliver when paid,
-- and later did not, "does not cheat".
DECLARE `My dealing` HAS
    `I deceived the other person on purpose, including by dishonestly concealing facts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I induced them to deliver property to anyone, or to consent that anyone keep property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I induced them to make, alter or destroy a valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my intention` IS A `My intention as to property`
    `I intended by the deception an advantage to me or another, or a detriment to them or another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds it so slight that no reasonable person would complain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I intentionally induced them to do or omit something they would not have done if not deceived` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that act or omission caused or was likely to cause harm to someone in body, mind, reputation or property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deception was conducted mainly by Internet, telephone, television, radio or other communication technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has declared by Gazette order that method is not remote communication` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I cheated` d IF
        d's `I deceived the other person on purpose, including by dishonestly concealing facts`
    AND (       d's `I induced them to deliver property to anyone, or to consent that anyone keep property`
            AND (    `Did I act dishonestly` (d's `my intention`)
                 OR  `Did I act fraudulently` (d's `I deceived the other person on purpose, including by dishonestly concealing facts`)
                                              (d's `I intended by the deception an advantage to me or another, or a detriment to them or another`)
                                              (d's `the court finds it so slight that no reasonable person would complain`))
         OR     d's `I intentionally induced them to do or omit something they would not have done if not deceived`
            AND d's `that act or omission caused or was likely to cause harm to someone in body, mind, reputation or property`)

-- s 416B(1): to "cheat by remote communication" is to cheat where "the deception is conducted mainly by way of remote communication";
-- (2) "remote communication" is through the Internet, telephone or other device, television or radio, or other technology, "but
-- excludes any specific system or method ... that the Minister, by order in the Gazette, declares is not remote communication". No
-- such order is deposited: an input.
GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I cheat by remote communication` d IF
        `Have I cheated` d
    AND d's `the deception was conducted mainly by Internet, telephone, television, radio or other communication technology`
    AND NOT d's `the Minister has declared by Gazette order that method is not remote communication`

-- s 417: "Whoever cheats". s 420(1): "Whoever cheats and thereby DISHONESTLY induces the person deceived to deliver ... any property
-- to any person, or to make, alter or destroy ... a valuable security"; (2) the same "by remote communication". s 420 needs
-- dishonesty: cheating done fraudulently but not dishonestly stays under s 417. NOTHING means I have not cheated.
GIVEN d IS A `My dealing`
GIVETH A MAYBE Section
`Which section punishes my cheating` d MEANS
    IF NOT `Have I cheated` d
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF     `Did I act dishonestly` (d's `my intention`)
            AND (   d's `I induced them to deliver property to anyone, or to consent that anyone keep property`
                 OR d's `I induced them to make, alter or destroy a valuable security`)
         THEN IF `Did I cheat by remote communication` d
              THEN JUST `section 420(2)`
              ELSE JUST `section 420(1)`
         ELSE JUST `section 417`

§§ `ss 319 to 326, 334 to 335 -- hurt and grievous hurt`

-- s 319: "Whoever causes bodily pain, disease or infirmity to any person is said to cause hurt." Explanation: causing
-- unconsciousness is hurt. s 321: whoever acts "with the intention of thereby causing hurt ..., or with the knowledge that he is
-- likely thereby to cause hurt", and does cause it, "voluntarily" causes hurt.
-- s 320: the "grievous" kinds "only": (a) emasculation; (aa) death; (b) permanent privation of the sight of either eye; (c) of the
-- hearing of either ear; (d) privation of any member or joint; (e) destruction or permanent impairing of a member or joint;
-- (f) permanent disfiguration of the head or face; (g) fracture or dislocation of a bone; (h) "any hurt which endangers life, or which
-- causes the sufferer to be, during the space of 20 days, in severe bodily pain, or unable to follow his ordinary pursuits";
-- (i) non-consensual penetration causing severe bodily pain. "During the space of 20 days" is read as 20 days or more (an inference).
DECLARE Injury IS ONE OF
    `pain, bruises or cuts with no lasting harm`
    `emasculation`
    `death`
    `permanent loss of the sight of an eye`
    `permanent loss of the hearing of an ear`
    `loss of a member or joint`
    `destruction or permanent impairing of a member or joint`
    `permanent disfiguration of the head or face`
    `a fracture or dislocation of a bone`
    `penetration without consent causing severe bodily pain`

-- The weapons and means of ss 324 and 326: "any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or any instrument which, used as a weapon
-- of offence, is likely to cause death, or ... fire or any heated substance, ... poison or any corrosive substance, ... any explosive
-- substance, ... any substance which it is harmful to the human body to inhale, to swallow, or to receive into the blood, or ... any
-- animal". Asked as one fact.
-- ss 334, 334A, 335: hurt "on grave and sudden provocation, if he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any
-- person other than the person who gave the provocation" (s 335 says "grievous hurt" in that last limb; this encoding asks the
-- narrower s 334 fact for all three -- a simplification). Explanation to s 335: subject "to the same provisos as exception 1 of
-- section 300". Whether the provocation was grave and sudden within those provisos is the court's finding: an input.
DECLARE `My blow` HAS
    `I caused someone bodily pain, disease, infirmity or unconsciousness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I intended to cause hurt, or knew I was likely to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worst injury I caused` IS AN Injury
    `the days the person hurt was in severe bodily pain or unable to follow ordinary pursuits` IS A NUMBER
    `the hurt endangered life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I intended grievous hurt of some kind, or knew I was likely to cause it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I used a weapon or means named in sections 324 and 326` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds I acted on grave and sudden provocation within the provisos to Exception 1 of section 300` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I neither intended nor knew I was likely to hurt anyone but the person who provoked me` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN b IS A `My blow`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I voluntarily caused hurt` b IF
        b's `I caused someone bodily pain, disease, infirmity or unconsciousness`
    AND b's `I intended to cause hurt, or knew I was likely to`

GIVEN b IS A `My blow`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the hurt I caused grievous` b IF
        b's `I caused someone bodily pain, disease, infirmity or unconsciousness`
    AND (   b's `the hurt endangered life`
         OR b's `the days the person hurt was in severe bodily pain or unable to follow ordinary pursuits` AT LEAST 20
         OR CONSIDER b's `the worst injury I caused`
            WHEN `pain, bruises or cuts with no lasting harm` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 322: grievous hurt is caused "voluntarily" only if "the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is
-- grievous hurt, and ... the hurt which he causes is grievous hurt"; Explanation: intending one kind and causing another still counts.
-- s 323 "except in the case provided for by section 323A or 334"; s 323A: hurt intended is not grievous "but the hurt which he actually
-- causes is grievous"; s 324 "except in the case provided for by section 334"; s 325 "except in the case provided for by section 323A,
-- 334A or 335"; s 326 "except in the case provided for by section 335". s 334A: on provocation, intended hurt not grievous but caused
-- grievous; s 335: grievous hurt voluntarily caused on provocation.
-- Two readings taken (inferences, see NOTES.md): provocation displaces every non-provocation section, s 324 included, though s 324
-- excepts only s 334; and a weapon used to cause grievous hurt that was not intended falls under s 324 (which does not except s 323A),
-- the heavier of the two that reach it. Intending grievous hurt but causing only simple hurt is s 323 (or s 324), not s 325.
-- NOTHING means I have not voluntarily caused hurt.
GIVEN b IS A `My blow`
GIVETH A MAYBE Section
`Which section punishes the hurt I caused` b MEANS
    IF NOT `Have I voluntarily caused hurt` b
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE BRANCH
          IF     b's `the court finds I acted on grave and sudden provocation within the provisos to Exception 1 of section 300`
             AND b's `I neither intended nor knew I was likely to hurt anyone but the person who provoked me`
          THEN IF `Is the hurt I caused grievous` b
               THEN IF b's `I intended grievous hurt of some kind, or knew I was likely to cause it`
                    THEN JUST `section 335`
                    ELSE JUST `section 334A`
               ELSE JUST `section 334`
          IF     `Is the hurt I caused grievous` b
             AND b's `I intended grievous hurt of some kind, or knew I was likely to cause it`
          THEN IF b's `I used a weapon or means named in sections 324 and 326`
               THEN JUST `section 326`
               ELSE JUST `section 325`
          IF b's `I used a weapon or means named in sections 324 and 326`
          THEN JUST `section 324`
          IF `Is the hurt I caused grievous` b
          THEN JUST `section 323A`
          OTHERWISE JUST `section 323`

§§ `ss 503, 506, 507 -- criminal intimidation`

-- s 503: "Whoever threatens another with any injury to his person, reputation or property, or to the person or reputation of any one
-- in whom that person is interested, with intent to cause alarm to that person, or to cause that person to do any act which he is not
-- legally bound to do, or to omit to do any act which that person is legally entitled to do, as the means of avoiding the execution of
-- such threat, commits criminal intimidation." Explanation: a threat to the reputation of a deceased person one is interested in counts.
DECLARE `Threatened harm` IS ONE OF
    `death`
    `grievous hurt`
    `destruction of property by fire`
    `an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment of 7 years or more`
    `some other injury`

DECLARE `My threat` HAS
    `I threatened injury to their person, reputation or property, or to the person or reputation of someone they are interested in` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I intended to alarm them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I intended to make them do what they were not legally bound to do, or omit what they were entitled to do, to avoid the threat` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what I threatened` IS A `Threatened harm`
    `I made it anonymously, or took precautions to conceal my name or abode` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN m IS A `My threat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed criminal intimidation` m IF
        m's `I threatened injury to their person, reputation or property, or to the person or reputation of someone they are interested in`
    AND (   m's `I intended to alarm them`
         OR m's `I intended to make them do what they were not legally bound to do, or omit what they were entitled to do, to avoid the threat`)

-- s 506: "2 years, or with fine, or with both; and if the threat is to cause death or grievous hurt, or to cause the destruction of any
-- property by fire, or to cause an offence punishable with death or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years or more",
-- 10 years, or fine, or both. NOTHING means no criminal intimidation.
GIVEN m IS A `My threat`
GIVETH A MAYBE Section
`Which section punishes my threat` m MEANS
    IF NOT `Have I committed criminal intimidation` m
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER m's `what I threatened`
         WHEN `some other injury` THEN JUST `section 506`
         OTHERWISE JUST `section 506, threat of death, grievous hurt, fire or a serious offence`

-- s 507: by "an anonymous communication, or by having taken precautions to conceal the name or abode of the person from whom the threat
-- comes", a further 2 years "in addition to the punishment provided for the offence by section 506". NOTHING means no criminal
-- intimidation.
GIVEN m IS A `My threat`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for my threat, in months` m MEANS
    CONSIDER `Which section punishes my threat` m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST s THEN JUST (    `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for, in months, under` s
                          PLUS IF m's `I made it anonymously, or took precautions to conceal my name or abode` THEN 24 ELSE 0)

§§ `ss 96 to 103, 106A -- private defence of the body`

-- s 96: "Nothing is an offence which is done in the exercise of the right of private defence." s 97(a): every person may defend "his
-- own body, and the body of any other person, against any offence affecting the human body". s 98(1): the right "does not extend to
-- the inflicting of more harm than it is reasonably necessary"; (2) there is none where "there is reasonable opportunity to have
-- recourse to the protection of a public authority". s 101: it starts when the defender "reasonably believes that there is danger to
-- the body ... arising from any act which is an offence against the human body or an attempt or a threat to commit the offence" and
-- continues "as long as the belief of danger ... continues". s 102: it extends to "the voluntary causing of death to the assailant"
-- only against an assault the defender reasonably believes will otherwise cause (a) death or (b) grievous hurt, or is done with intent
-- of (c) rape, (d) penile penetration under s 376(2), (e) kidnapping or abducting, or (f) wrongful confinement with no expected
-- recourse to a public authority; s 103: otherwise it extends to "any harm other than death". s 106A: there is none against a public
-- servant acting in good faith under colour of office, or one acting by such a public servant's direction, unless the act causes a
-- reasonable belief "that death or grievous hurt would result"; Explanations: only if the defender knew or had reason to believe who
-- the assailant was. Necessity and excess are the court's findings: inputs. s 99 (the same right against a child, a person of unsound
-- mind or a mistaken assailant) means nothing below asks about the assailant's own guilt.
DECLARE `Feared outcome` IS ONE OF
    `my death or another's`
    `grievous hurt`
    `rape`
    `penile penetration as described in section 376(2)`
    `kidnapping or abduction`
    `wrongful confinement with no expected recourse to a public authority`
    `some lesser harm`

DECLARE `My defence` HAS
    `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that belief still held when I acted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I caused the assailant's death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring` IS A `Feared outcome`
    `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `Feared outcome`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 102 let me go as far as causing death` f IF
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `some lesser harm` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN f IS A `Feared outcome`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I fear death or grievous hurt` f IF
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `my death or another's` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `grievous hurt` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN p IS A `My defence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I did no offence because it was private defence` p IF
        p's `I reasonably believed there was danger to my body or another's from an offence against the body, or an attempt or threat of one`
    AND p's `that belief still held when I acted`
    AND NOT p's `the court finds I had a reasonable opportunity to seek the protection of a public authority`
    AND NOT p's `the court finds I inflicted more harm than was reasonably necessary`
    AND (   NOT p's `I caused the assailant's death`
         OR `Does section 102 let me go as far as causing death` (p's `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring`))
    AND (   NOT p's `I knew or had reason to believe the assailant was a public servant acting in good faith in office, or by such a direction`
         OR `Did I fear death or grievous hurt` (p's `what I reasonably believed the assault would bring`))

§§ `s 512 -- an attempt`

-- s 512(1): an attempt at an offence "punishable ... with death or imprisonment for life" is punished, "where no express provision is
-- made", with imprisonment up to 20 years "and shall also be liable to fine or to caning". (2) any other attempt: "such punishment as
-- is prescribed for that offence"; (3) where that punishment includes "a specified minimum sentence or a mandatory minimum sentence of
-- imprisonment or fine or caning", the court "shall not be bound to impose" it, up to the maximum. None of the sections in this table
-- makes express provision for its own attempt (as read). Whether mandatory imprisonment with no stated minimum term is "a mandatory
-- minimum sentence of imprisonment" is not settled by the text; this encoding relaxes only the stated minimum (the 6 strokes of
-- s 420(2)) and keeps the mandatory imprisonment flag as it is (an inference, see NOTES.md).
GIVEN c IS A Caning
GIVETH A Caning
`relaxed` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `caning of at least` n THEN `caning at the court's discretion`
    OTHERWISE c

GIVEN s IS A Section
GIVETH A Punishment
`What is the most I can be punished with for attempting the offence under` s MEANS
    IF `Can I be imprisoned for life under` s
    THEN `Punishment` OF FALSE, 240, TRUE, `a fine with no maximum stated in the Code`, `caning at the court's discretion`
    ELSE `Punishment` OF FALSE,
                         `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for, in months, under` s,
                         `Must the court imprison me if I am convicted under` s,
                         `What fine can I be made to pay under` s,
                         `relaxed` (`Can I be caned under` s)
